us verifiers' lives much easier compared to the completely unstructured legacy EVM code. The legacy EVM example can be seen in our post Finding Auxdatas in the Bytecode . However as of the current specification, the metadata is still not fully isolated from the contract code as there is no separate section for that information. Current compiler implementations put the metadata in the data_section of EOF and this unfortunately does affect the contract's code. That's why we are proposing a separate metadata_section in the EVM Object Format that cannot be reached by the EVM and any changes to that will not affect the contract's code. If this is implemented, verifiers can completely ignore the metadata parts of a container, and won't have to look for workarounds. You can check our proposal EIP-7834
